   "q_en": "<p>A train moving with a speed of 72 km/h crosses a man moving in a car in opposite direction in 6 seconds. If the length of the train is 168 meters, then find the speed of the car. </p>",
   "q_hi": "<p>72 km/h &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2352;&#2361;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; 6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 168 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; (m) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>",
   "options_en": [
    "10 m/s",
    "8 m/s",
    "12 m/s",
    "9 m/s"
   ],
   "options_hi": [
    "10 m/s",
    "8 m/s",
    "12 m/s",
    "9 m/s"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "solution_en": "<p>Speed of train = 72 km/h = 72 * 5/18 m/s = 20 m/s</p><p>Let speed of car = s m/s</p><p>Since the train and the car are moving in opposite direction, so their relative speed = (20 + s) m/s</p><p>Now, time taken by the train to cross the man in the car = length of train/relative speed </p><p>6 = 168/(20 + s)</p><p>20 + s = 28</p><p><b>s = 8</b></p>",
   "solution_hi": "<p>Speed of train = 72 km/h = 72 * 5/18 m/s = 20 m/s</p><p>Let speed of car = s m/s</p><p>Since the train and the car are moving in opposite direction, so their relative speed = (20 + s) m/s</p><p>Now, time taken by the train to cross the man in the car = length of train/relative speed </p><p>6 = 168/(20 + s)</p><p>20 + s = 28</p><p><b>s = 8</b></p>",
