   "q_en": "<p>The speed of train A is 96 km/h, and it is 760 meters long, then what is the total time taken by train A to cross a 440 meters long bridge and another 1160 meters long train B which is running in the opposite direction at 64 km/h?</p>",
   "q_hi": "<p>&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; A &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; 96 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2351;&#2361; 760 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 440 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2346;&#2369;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; 64 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; 1160 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; B &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>",
   "options_en": [
    "81.6 seconds",
    "80.2 seconds",
    "84.4 seconds",
    "88.2 seconds"
   ],
   "options_hi": [
    "81.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;",
    "80.2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;",
    "84.4 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;",
    "88.2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"
   ],
   "answer": 3,
   "solution_en": "<p>Time taken to cross the bridge by train A = (760 + 440)/(96 * 5/18) = 45 seconds</p><p>Time taken to cross train B by train A = (760 + 1160)/((96 + 64) * 5/18) = 43.2 seconds</p><p>So, total time = 45 + 43.2 = 88.2 seconds</p>",
